(Planned Early Delivery in Treated Hypertensive Pregnancy: Maternal and Neonatal Outcomes) Tj
T*
(from the TERM-HYP Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Four hundred three pregnant women with hypertensive disorders at term were randomized to) Tj
T*
(either planned delivery at 38 weeks \(n = 201\) or standard management \(n = 202\). Baseline) Tj
T*
(characteristics were balanced; most participants had well-controlled blood pressure on) Tj
T*
(antihypertensive therapy. The planned early delivery group delivered a median of 0.9 weeks) Tj
T*
(earlier \(38.4 versus 39.3 weeks gestation\). Severe maternal complications including) Tj
T*
(hypertensive emergency, maternal death, or ICU admission occurred in 13% of the early) Tj
T*
(delivery group and 12% of the standard management group \(adjusted risk ratio 1.14, 95% CI) Tj
T*
(0.70-1.86\). Neonatal intensive care admission for 4 or more hours occurred in 7% of both) Tj
T*
(groups \(adjusted risk difference -0.01, 95% CI -0.06 to +0.07\), meeting non-inferiority) Tj
T*
(criteria. Cesarean delivery rates were 29% versus 36% \(adjusted risk ratio 0.79, 95% CI) Tj
T*
(0.59-1.06\). No serious adverse events were reported. Planned delivery at 38 weeks offers a) Tj
T*
(safe alternative in hypertensive pregnancy.) Tj
